# Using the Kaldor‐Hicks Tableau Format for Cost‐Benefit Analysis and Policy Evaluation

**Authors:** K. Krutilla

## Abstract
This note describes the Kaldor-Hicks (KH) tableau format as a framework for distributional accounting in cost-benefit analysis and policy evaluation. The KH tableau format can serve as a heuristic aid for teaching microeconomics-based policy analysis, and offer insight to policy analysts and decisionmakers beyond conventional efficiency analysis. © 2005 by the Association for Public Policy Analysis and Management

